    "result_text": "All 282 tests pass, including the new cp16 test. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, the response now includes an integer `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of *other* owners that already shared the new owner's last name at the moment of creation.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring how `membershipNumber` / `customerCode` / `membershipTier` work):\n\n1. **`CountNamesakes`** (new function class) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `lastName` equals the new owner's, and records it on the entity. It runs before `save`, so the count correctly excludes the owner being created.\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `countNamesakes` step into the pipeline (after `enforceCityLimit`, before `assignMembership`), under the same `transaction` governance.\n3. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` field with `@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")` plus getter/setter, so the value is persisted and frozen at creation time (and read back on later GETs).\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `namesake_count INTEGER` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\nThe new `Cp16Tests` (first owner with a surname \u2192 0, second \u2192 1) passes, and the full suite remains green.",
